hadiths[31]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18433","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Simak narrated to me, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever swears an oath and sees better than it, let him do what is better."
"18434","Yahya ibn Said and Waki narrated to us, from Zakariyya, Waki said: From Amir, and Yahya said in his hadith: Amir narrated to me, he said: Adi ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting with the mirad, and he said: What you strike with its sharp edge, eat it, and what you strike with its side is beaten dead, and I asked him about hunting with a dog, Waki said: When you send your dog and mention the name of Allah, eat, and he said: Whatever it holds for you and does not eat from, eat it, for its catching is its slaughter, and if you find with your dog another dog and fear it caught it with yours and killed it, do not eat, for you mentioned the name of Allah over your dog and did not mention it over another."
"18435","Waki and Abu Muawiyah al-Mana narrated to us, they said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim al-Tai who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you but his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will speak to him with no interpreter between him and Him, then he will look to his right and see only what he sent forth, and he will look to his left and see only what he sent forth, and he will look before him and the Fire will face him, so whoever among you is able to shield himself from the Fire even with half a date, let him do so."
"18436","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Rufay, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Adi ibn Hatim that a man gave a sermon before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger is rightly guided, and whoever disobeys them both is astray, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an evil preacher you are, say: And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger."
"18437","Waki narrated to us, Sadan al-Juhani narrated to us, from Ibn Khalifah al-Tai, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever among you is able to shield himself from the Fire, let him give charity even with half a date, and whoever does not find, then with a good word."
"18438","Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting with the mirad, and he said: Do not eat unless it pierces."
"18439","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak, from Murayy ibn Qatari, from Adi ibn Hatim al-Tai who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we hunt game and find no knife except sharp stones and a split stick, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cause the blood to flow with whatever you wish and mention the name of Allah."
"18440","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr, the freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, narrating from Adi ibn Hatim who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath and sees another better than it, let him do what is better and expiate his oath."
"18441","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Miqal, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you is able to shield himself from the Fire even with half a date, let him do so."
"18442","Abd al-Rahman and Ibn Jafar both said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Fire, Ibn Jafar said: So he sought refuge from it and turned his face aside, then said: Fear the Fire even with half a date, and if you do not find, then with a good word."
"18443","Abd al-Rahman and Ibn Jafar both said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhill ibn Khalifah, Abd al-Rahman said: I heard Adi ibn Hatim say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear the Fire even with half a date, and if you do not find, then with a good word, and Ibn Jafar said: Then with a word."
"18444","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Said ibn Masruq who said: al-Shabi narrated to us, he said: I heard Adi ibn Hatim, and he was a neighbor to us, or a guest and tied up at al-Nahrayn, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I send my dog and find with my dog another dog that has caught, and I do not know which of them caught, he said: Do not eat, for you named over your dog and did not name over another."
"18445","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of that."
"18446","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay informed me, he said: I heard Tamim ibn Tarafah al-Tai narrating from Adi ibn Hatim who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath and sees another better than it, let him do what is better and leave his oath."
"18447","Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he taught me Islam and described the prayer to me and how I should pray each prayer at its time, then he said to me: How will you be, O son of Hatim, when you ride from the palaces of Yemen fearing none but Allah until you descend at the palaces of al-Hirah, I said: O Messenger of Allah, then where will the horsemen of Tayyi and its men be, he said: Allah will suffice you against Tayyi and others besides them, I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people who hunt with these dogs and falcons, so what is lawful for us of them, he said: Lawful for you is what you teach of hunting creatures as trainers, teaching them from what Allah taught you, so eat from what they hold for you and mention the name of Allah over it, so whatever you train of dog or falcon, then send and mention the name of Allah over it, eat from what it holds for you, I said: Even if it kills, he said: Even if it kills and eats nothing from it, for it held it for you, I said: What if other dogs mix with our dogs when we send them, he said: Do not eat until you know that your dog is the one that held it for you, I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people who shoot with the mirad, so what is lawful for us, he said: Do not eat what you strike with the mirad except what you slaughter properly."
"18448","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my land is a land of hunting, he said: When you send your dog and name, eat what your dog holds for you even if it kills, but if it eats from it do not eat, for it held it for itself, and when you send your dog and it is joined by dogs over which you did not name, do not eat, for you do not know which of them killed it."
"18449","Yazid informed us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Ubaydah, from a man who said: I said to Adi ibn Hatim: A hadith reached me from you that I wish to hear from you, he said: Yes, when the emergence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached me I hated his emergence with intense hatred, and I left until I reached the direction of the Romans, and he said, meaning Yazid, at Baghdad, until I came to Caesar, and I hated that place of mine more intensely than my hatred of his emergence, and I said: By Allah, if I were to come to this man, if he is a liar he will not harm me, and if he is truthful I will know, so I came and went to him, and when I arrived the people said: Adi ibn Hatim, Adi ibn Hatim, so I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said to me: O Adi ibn Hatim, accept Islam and you will be safe, three times, I said: I am upon a religion, he said: I know your religion better than you, so I said: Are you more knowledgeable of my religion than I, he said: Yes, are you not of al-Rakusiyyah while you eat a quarter of your peoples spoils, I said: Yes, he said: For this is not lawful for you in your religion, and he had barely said it when I submitted to it, then he said: Indeed I know what prevents you from Islam, you say: Only the weak of the people and those without strength followed him, while the Arabs have united against them, do you know al-Hirah, I said: I have not seen it but I have heard of it, he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah will certainly complete this matter until a woman traveler leaves al-Hirah and circles the House with no protection from anyone, and the treasures of Khosrau ibn Hurmuz will certainly be opened, I said: Khosrau ibn Hurmuz, he said: Yes, Khosrau ibn Hurmuz, and wealth will certainly be lavished until none accepts it, Adi ibn Hatim said: So here is the woman traveler leaving al-Hirah and circling the House with no protection, and I was among those who opened the treasures of Khosrau ibn Hurmuz, and by Him in Whose Hand is my soul the third will surely be, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it."
"18450","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn al-Musayyir al-Tai who said: Muhill al-Tai informed me, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: Whoever leads us should complete the bowing and prostration, for among us are the weak and the old and the sick and the passerby and the needy, thus we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"18451","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb who said: I heard Murayy ibn Qatari who said: I heard Adi ibn Hatim who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father used to keep ties of kinship and do such and such, he said: Your father sought a matter and attained it, meaning remembrance, I said: I ask you about food I do not leave except from scruple, he said: Do not leave anything in which you resemble Christianity, I said: I send my dog and it catches game, and I have nothing with me to slaughter it with, so I slaughter it with a sharp stone and a stick, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cause the blood to flow with whatever you wish and mention the name of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"18452","Husayn narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and he mentioned it with its chain, except that he said: I heard Murayy ibn Qatari al-Tai, and he said: Your father sought a matter and attained it, Simak said: Meaning remembrance."
"18453","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, and he mentioned it from the place of hunting, and he said: Cause the blood to flow."
"18454","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Tamim ibn Tarafah who said: I heard Adi ibn Hatim, and a man came to him asking him for a hundred dirhams, and he said: You ask me for a hundred dirhams while I am the son of Hatim, by Allah I will not give you, then he said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever swears an oath then sees another better than it, let him do what is better."
"18455","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I said: O Messenger of Allah, we send our trained dogs, he said: Eat, I said: Even if it kills, he said: Even if it kills, so long as no other dogs join them, I said: We shoot with the mirad, he said: If it pierces, eat, and if it strikes with its side, do not eat."
"18456","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Murayy ibn Qatari, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting that I hunt, he said: Cause the blood to flow with whatever you wish and mention the name of Allah and eat."
"18457","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from a man who said, meaning: I used to ask the people about the hadith of Adi ibn Hatim while he was beside me and I did not ask him, so I went to him and asked him, and he said: Yes, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent when he was sent, then he mentioned the hadith."
"18458","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Ibn Hudhayfah who said: I used to narrate a hadith from Adi ibn Hatim, and I said: Here is Adi ibn Hatim in the district of Kufah, if only I went to him and I myself heard it from him, so I went to him and said: I used to narrate a hadith from you and I wanted to be the one to hear it from you, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent I fled until I was in the farthest Romans, then he mentioned the hadith."
"18459","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Bayan, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I said: We are people who hunt with these dogs, he said: When you send your trained dogs and mention the name of Allah, eat from what they hold for you even if they kill, unless the dog eats, for if it eats do not eat, for I fear it held it for itself, and if it is joined by other dogs, do not eat."
"18460","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Ibn Miqal, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear the Fire, and he turned his face aside until we thought he was looking at it, then he said: Fear the Fire, and he turned his face aside, he said it two or three times: Fear the Fire even with half a date, and if you do not find, then with a good word."
"18461","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Miqal, from Adi ibn Hatim al-Tai who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear the Fire even with half a date."
"18462","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay narrating, he said: I heard Tamim ibn Tarafah narrating from Adi ibn Hatim who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever swears an oath then sees another better than it, let him do what is better and leave his oath."
"18463","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq who said: Fear the Fire and do good and act, for I heard Abd Allah ibn Miqal say: I heard Adi ibn Hatim say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fear the Fire even with half a date."
